From a1132a6018cb1b2c1bf7b3ba755ef394d74a4d6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:38:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0287 -- optional pre-video hold so the launcher banner
 stays readable

The QA sweeps print "[n/10] CELL <name> -- listen for X" and then start the
engine immediately, so on fast hardware the banner flashes past before the
operator can read what the next cell is testing.

DOS offers no timed wait here: CHOICE.COM is absent on the reference machine,
PAUSE needs a keypress and the sweeps are unattended, and a BAT busy-loop
would run for wildly different durations on a Pentium OverDrive versus a 486
-- the one thing a benchmark harness must not introduce. Doing it in the
engine is the only way to get a real, CPU-independent delay.

SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BANNER_DELAY_MS (or DOSKUTSU_BANNER_DELAY_MS), milliseconds,
ceiling 60 s, absent/0 = no delay so default behaviour is unchanged. Runs at
the top of main() before SDL_Init and before any logic tick, so it cannot
perturb a measurement: nothing has been timed yet and the TAS clock has not
started. The sweeps set it to 10000 once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 43843cab..a66dfcd7 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -1662,6 +1662,32 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
   // Logged at engine exit via emit_run_manifest().
   _runmanifest_boot_time = std::time(nullptr);
 
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0287): optional hold before the engine takes the screen,
+  // so the DOS-side banner the launcher just printed stays readable.
+  //
+  // The QA sweeps print "[n/10] CELL <name> -- listen for X" and then start
+  // the engine immediately, which on fast hardware flashes past. DOS has no
+  // timed wait: CHOICE.COM is absent on the reference machine, PAUSE needs a
+  // keypress (the sweeps are unattended), and a BAT busy-loop would run for
+  // wildly different durations on a Pentium OverDrive versus a 486. Doing it
+  // here is the only way to get a real, CPU-independent delay.
+  //
+  // Runs before SDL_Init and before any tick, so it cannot touch a benchmark:
+  // no logic tick has happened and the TAS clock has not started.
+  {
+    const char *bd = std::getenv("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BANNER_DELAY_MS");
+    if (!bd) bd = std::getenv("DOSKUTSU_BANNER_DELAY_MS");
+    if (bd && bd[0])
+    {
+      long ms = std::strtol(bd, nullptr, 10);
+      if (ms > 0)
+      {
+        if (ms > 60000) ms = 60000;   // sanity ceiling
+        SDL_Delay((Uint32)ms);
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   // DOS-PORT (patch 0216): load DOSKUTSU.CFG into the environment before any
   // getenv / SDL_GetHint read of a config key (SDL_GetHint falls back to the
   // env var of the same name). The file is an alternate source for the SAME
